    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="P8_Ann_84">
      <bpmn:text>Clinical decision only: administrative and finance staff must not decide whether the patient can continue treatment.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="P13_TextAnnotation_0dlfeg7">
      <bpmn:text>This letter covers visit notes, diagnosis, test findings, treatment choices and future check-up plans. The doctor also writes who should receive this letter.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="P13_TextAnnotation_1rnf7g3">
      <bpmn:text>You may fix small formatting mistakes, but never change its medical meaning.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="P13_TextAnnotation_0nuc5th">
      <bpmn:text>all reminders, replies and previous problem-escalation records</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="LinkNotationLegend">
      <bpmn:text>Same-file navigation: matching INBOX, E01–E13 and Lxx link codes continue within this process. Links do not start or end a process and do not wait for another message. All 17 workflow groups remain in this BPMN.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
